<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Entitlements: none requested.

  `com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit` was requested here, and is deliberately NOT,
  pending D-047. Architecture §3.4 and Compliance both recommend shipping iteration-1 without it,
  and the measured budget agrees: the ~396 MB of weights are clean, file-backed pages that jetsam
  charges very little of, so what is actually charged is the KV cache (~115 MB at 2048 tokens,
  q8_0), the compute buffer (~28 MiB, D-028) and the app itself — about 321 MB of footprint against
  a conservative ~1.3 GB ceiling. Insurance we do not need is still a claim we have to justify at
  review, and it contradicts C3's habit of asking for nothing.

  If a future profile ships a larger model this becomes load-bearing, and must be VERIFIED on a
  3-4 GB device before that profile is committed to (D-050). Re-add it here, with the measurement
  that justified it.

  `com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing` is likewise not requested: it matters for
  mapping files near the address-space cap, which 400 MB is nowhere near.

  No keychain group, no App Groups, no push, no Siri, no associated domains.

  UNVERIFIED: not built, not signed, not submitted.

  spine: C2, C3
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
